lesson: 64
title: How many more to make a full ten
stars: 0
explain: To find how many more make a round number, count on from what you have to that number.
explain: You can also take away: to make 30 from 24, think 30 - 24 = 6. Check: 24 + 6 = 30.
explain: To make 10 from 7 you need 3, because 7 and 3 make 10.
vars: a=name t=thing c=1..10 n=1..99
let: m = 10 * c
need: n < m
need: n >= 2
answer: m - n
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. How many more {t} does {a.he} need to have {m}?
exercise: A box holds {m} {t}. There are {n} {t} in it now. How many more {t} fit in the box?
exercise: {a} wants to collect {m} {t}. {a.He} already has {n}. How many more must {a.he} collect?
exercise: What number must be added to {n} to make {m}?
exercise: {a} has read {n} pages of a {m}-page book. How many pages are left to read?
test: {m} {t} are needed for a game, but only {n} are on the table. How many are missing?
test: To reach {m}, how much is still needed after {n}?
test: {a}'s jar fits exactly {m} {t}. If {n} are inside, how many more go in before it is full?
exercise: How many more than {n} is {m}?
exercise: {a} wants to buy a game that costs {m} dollars. {a.He} has saved {n} dollars. How many more dollars does {a.he} need?
exercise: {n} + ? = {m}. What is the missing number?
exercise: A bus in London has {m} seats. {n} seats are taken. How many seats are still free?
exercise: {a} is making a necklace of {m} beads. {a.He} has threaded {n}. How many beads are still to go?
exercise: {a} needs {m} {t} for a party and has {n} so far. How many {t} is {a.he} still short?
exercise: A team in Auckland must plant {m} trees. They have planted {n} trees. How many trees are left to plant?
exercise: Count on from {n.words} to {m}. How many steps is that?
test: {m} is the target and {a} is at {n}. How big is the gap?
test: A carton in a Sydney shop holds {m} {t} when full. It holds {n} right now. How many {t} would fill it up?
test: How much less than {m} is {n}?
test: {a} has scored {n} points in a computer game. The next level starts at {m} points. How many more points must {a.he} win?
test: A tray in a Canadian bakery has places for {m} rolls, and {n} places are filled. How many places are empty?
test: Fill in the blank: {m} = {n} + ___.
exercise: got {n} {t}, need {m}. how many more i need
exercise: box takes {m} {t}, {n} in it already, how many more fit
exercise: {a} wants {m} {t} — had {n+1}, no sorry, {n}. how many more to get?
exercise: Kai says {m} take away {n} is {m+n}. nah thats adding, whats the real answer
