test: {n} {t} in the jar, wanna get it to {m}. how many to chuck in
test: {a} asks how many to go from {n} up to {m}. what u tell {a.him}
exam: Whereas a receptacle has a capacity of {m} {t} and presently contains {n}, determine the number of additional {t} required to fill it completely.
exam: Ascertain the quantity which, when added to {n}, yields precisely {m}.
exam: It is given that {a} possesses {n} {t}. Determine the deficiency in respect of a holding of {m} {t}.
exam: State the number of further {t} that must be acquired by {a}, who holds {n}, in order that {a.his} holding attain {m.words}.
exercise: Mrs Lee, the school cook, passed away, and the class wants to buy flowers that cost {m} dollars. They have collected {n} dollars so far. How many more dollars do they need?
exercise: The rent this month is {m} dollars. Since {a}'s mum was laid off, the family only has {n} dollars. How many dollars are they short?
test: bloody hell {a}, your report says 'not working to full potential'. teacher wants {m} lines, you've done {n}. how many more, get on with it
